      },
      "text": "Lake Titicaca, Uros and Taquile"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "8e7f22c43d40a8af82cebd98ce196be56d41ac7640124366704238aa98ca9a90",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-79efc77a-b889-42c3-95a7-4d1a8db6bd09",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, you transfer to the port and head out onto Lake Titicaca. Many Peruvians consider the lake sacred, linking it to the origins of the Inca people and the legend of Manco Cápac.\n\nFirst, you visit the floating reed islands of the Uros. There are more than 40 islands, all built by the local people. During the tour, you learn about the community’s history and see how the islands are made. You can buy souvenirs and, if you like, take a ride in a traditional reed boat.\n\nYou then continue to Taquile Island, where the community maintains its own traditions, rules and crafts. The main settlement sits at around 3,950 metres above sea level. Taquile is especially well known for its weaving, which UNESCO recognised in 2005 as a Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity.\n\nYou have lunch on the island. After returning to Puno, you transfer to the airport and fly to Lima, where you are met and taken to your hotel."
    },
